Both GPU failures have one root cause in my shader change. The RT shadow dummy is 1x1, but the scene shader loads it at the full pixel coordinate. Out-of-range loads return 0, so every directional light goes dark. That is why the existing lighting tests fail. The test also used floor points at x = ±3, outside the view.

Fixes: clamp the traced-texture loads to the texture's size in `scene.hlsl`, and move the test occluders and sample points to x = ±1.2 so they are in view.
